 "findings": [
  "Greedy execution deadlocks in 30 of 65 admitted programs, always on the ancilla pool: later iterations take ancillas early and hold them, and the operations that would release them wait for an ancilla. Every program with several blocks or loops deadlocks, on every platform.",
  "Ordered acquisition never deadlocks and finishes 1.04 to 10 times sooner than the fixed timetable: a static timetable is safe but leaves most of the machine idle.",
  "Those speed-ups use only the VM's services. Whether the hardware can actually run such a schedule is the next example."
 ],
 "command": "node riscq/os/contention.mjs",
 "note": "All numbers are measured on QuantumOS's Lean model of RISC-Q control hardware (its cores, hubs and lanes are checked against RISC-Q's RTL cycle for cycle), on generated or published hardware designs. They are properties of that model, not of laboratory hardware.",
 "generated": "2026-11-25T14:58:38.418Z"
